  "what_is_not_claimed": "Balance and nothing more: every limit shown has zero contact margin, and the three-block gain disappears at any positive margin. No friction, no sliding or tipping dynamics (the moves in the video are quasi-static repositionings through balanced states), no rounded edges, uneven weights, deformation or 3-D effects. Nothing about real blocks, or about more than six blocks.",
  "verification_not_validation": "Every candidate contact pattern of one to six blocks with closed contact intervals is generated. A linear programme keeps those that exist with exactly their own contacts; the others exist only with extra contacts, and are covered by the richer pattern, or not at all. Each one kept is either solved by two separately written formulations, which reproduce the published values of Paterson and Zwick and Ainley's four-block closed form, or certified by branch and bound to have no balanced placement. The one- to four-block maxima carry a branch-and-bound upper bound within a stated gap. All of it reads the same idealisation. No physical stack is reproduced here.",
